Minor spoilers (about unicorn horns and black puddings)...

There's been some talk about having compiler flags to make nethack easier
for people who like to be spoiled. For example, the message "Nothing
happens" from a unicorn horn might be replaced by "You aren't suffering
from any ailments for the unicorn horn to cure" or even "None of your
abilities need restoration."

But what about a HARDER version with regards to messages? I'm not talking 
about the good suggestions about making the monsters in the second half of
the game less ignorable, but removing messages like "You feel very jumpy."
So, when you eat a black pudding, and want to know if you got poison
resistance or cold resistance, well, you can just go test it out! (Or drink
a potion of enlightenment.) Presumably you'd want to actually check on
disintegration resistance via a potion...

Another possibility would be to remove your automatic knowledge of your
armor class (which I have always thought ridiculous). I suppose this
could be replaced by messages you might get during combat like "Your
orcish helm seems to be defending you especially well". Of course, for the 
even harder level, you wouldn't get that, you'd just have to judge by hit 
point loss. In this way you wouldn't recognize rings of protection, either.

[Tangential note: why is weight, such an easily judgeable quantity in
real life, treated this way?]

Another is to remove your automatic ability to know if a monster is
peaceful or tame, and for you to be always asked if you want to attack
a monster that hasn't already attacked you (unless you're conflicted,
I suppose). I really don't see how a non-telepathic character can judge
the intentions of an acid blob.

So, mainly I'm seeking out humorous suggestions to make the game less
spoilery. To be precise, I'm NOT looking for suggestions like "Put a
Yeenoghu on every level," but rather "Make wands/scrolls of create monster
create one just outside the door, so you have to make the cause/effect
connection later on."

[Tangential note #2: why do you automatically recognize wands, but not
scrolls, of create monster?]					Allen K.


